WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:06.212
Hundredths are even smaller than tenths. One whole has one hundred of them.

00:06.662 --> 00:12.374
Each small square is one hundredth. We write it as zero point zero one.

00:12.824 --> 00:19.581
Shade thirty-seven squares. That is thirty-seven hundredths, or zero point three seven.

00:20.031 --> 00:27.358
The first digit after the point is tenths. The second digit is hundredths. In zero point three seven,

00:27.358 --> 00:30.550
there are three tenths and seven hundredths.

00:31.000 --> 00:37.741
Zero point four is the same as zero point four zero, because four tenths is forty hundredths.

00:37.741 --> 00:41.727
So zero point four is more than zero point three seven.
